          "label": "<p>According to FIGO, which set of values defines normal menstrual cycle parameters</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>According to FIGO, which set of values defines normal menstrual cycle parameters?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Frequency 21–35 days, duration 3–7 days, volume ≤100 mL</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>These older values have been superseded. The current FIGO parameters are: frequency 24–38 days, duration 4.5–8 days, and volume ≤80 mL per cycle.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Frequency 24–38 days, duration 2–5 days, volume ≤120 mL</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The frequency range is correct, but normal duration is 4.5–8 days and volume ≤80 mL — not the shorter duration or higher volume stated here.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Frequency 24–38 days, duration 4.5–8 days, volume ≤80 mL</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>These are the current FIGO-standardised normal parameters. Any deviation beyond these thresholds constitutes abnormal uterine bleeding.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Frequency 28–42 days, duration 5–10 days, volume ≤60 mL</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This overstates the upper frequency limit and duration while understating the volume threshold. The correct FIGO parameters are: 24–38 days, 4.5–8 days, ≤80 mL.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct FIGO normal menstrual parameters are: frequency 24–38 days, duration 4.5–8 days, and blood loss ≤80 mL per cycle. Memorise these — they define the boundary between normal and abnormal uterine bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. These FIGO parameters — frequency 24–38 days, duration 4.5–8 days, volume ≤80 mL — form the baseline against which abnormal uterine bleeding is defined."
                }
              ],
